=== 6. Code-path parity check: real ApiClient.getData (not the unit test's spy) ===
lib/api/api_client.dart:1109-1144 — with handleError:false + logError:false, handleResponse()
only ever emits a debug-only [NET] console trace (AppLogger.net, no Crashlytics) and returns
the raw Response untouched; it does NOT call ApiChecker.checkApi (which is the generic-[FAIL]
+ snackbar path). This confirms the SpyApiClient unit test's premise (repo's own branch is the
ONLY log source) matches the real production ApiClient, not just the test double.

=== 7. Pre-fix behavior confirmed via diff read (why this was noisy) ===
Before this fix, `_getConditionsWiseItems` called `getData(...)` with the DEFAULT
handleError:true. ApiChecker.checkApi (lib/api/api_checker.dart) unconditionally fires
AppLogger.failure -> [FAIL] + Crashlytics non-fatal for ANY non-200/non-1, AND shows the user
a generic snackbar (`showCustomSnackBar(response.statusText, ...)`) with the raw backend
message — meaning every sector back-out during the Pharmacy module home load surfaced a
spurious "Module id required" toast to real users, for a value (`conditionWiseProduct`) that
is never read by any widget (see #8).

